--------------------------- Changelog -----------------------------

1.0.a - UNRELEASED
Added - Campaign radial menu: hold a hotkey (B or either Ctrl key by default, or the middle or a side mouse button if you pick one) on the campaign map to open a wheel of abilities at the mouse, move onto one and release the key to use it. Tiles use the game's interface colour and chamfered borders, with narrow gaps between them, and show only icons unless Icons only is turned off. The tile under the mouse lights up in its icon's colour, lifts out of the ring and eases back when you move on. With Tinted tiles on, every usable tile shows a dim tint of its colour at rest. Resting on an ability shows its usual tooltip beside the wheel, F1 included, unless Ability tooltips is turned off. The game pauses while the wheel is open unless Pause while open is turned off, and Return cursor puts the pointer back where it was when you opened the wheel. The main wheel has 7 slots by default (1 to 10) and starts with Scavenge, Sustained Burn, Emergency Burn, Transponder, Go Dark, Sensor Burst and Interdiction Pulse, clockwise from the top. Hold the left mouse button on a slot for half a second to give it another of your fleet's abilities, empty it, or make it a submenu with its own icon and colour. Submenus can use 36 category icons, which take on the submenu's colour, or the icon of any ability your fleet has. Moving onto a submenu extends its tiles at once on an outer ring in that direction; move outward onto one to pick it, or back to the main ring or the center to close it. Submenus hold 5 abilities by default (1 to 10) and cannot contain another submenu. Abilities your fleet cannot use right now, cooling down included, turn grey, a cooling ability's sector fills from the outer edge inward until it is ready, and active ones pulse. A slot holding an ability your fleet does not have, including one from a mod you have since removed, looks and acts empty but remembers that ability for any save where you have it; putting something else in the slot replaces it. It plays the game's standard interface sounds. The wheel picks the tile in the mouse's direction however far out the mouse is, like a weapon wheel in a shooter; release in the center or press Escape to cancel. Turn off Select by direction to pick only the tile under the mouse, where releasing outside the ring also cancels
Note - Requires LunaLib. Change or clear the hotkeys, or pick a mouse button, under Hotkeys, the slot counts, Icons only, Tinted tiles, Ability tooltips, Return cursor, Pause while open and Select by direction under Wheel, and Expand hovered tile and Disable animations under Animation, in LunaLib's mod settings
Note - Your wheel layout is saved for every campaign. data/config/radial_menu.json only sets the starting abilities
Added - Loading screen tips covering radial menu controls, settings, slot editing, submenus, cancelling a selection and ability tooltips
